Track 3: Thermal Drift at the Terminus
- Story & Context: Deep in the dried salt bed of the Dead Siding, legend holds that the nomad ascetic Tariq vanished during the final sand-gale, dragging a bank of scavenged oscillators whose pitch drifted inexorably downward as the desert cold froze their circuitry. Pilgrims who track the abandoned rail-line to its physical end report hearing Tariq’s French horn still echoing from the petrified telegraph poles, tuned to a frequency that makes human teeth ache and matches the resonance of the tectonic plate. The air at the end of the line still reeks of dried iron and copper scale, throbbing with an impossible, endless low-end pulse that refuses to decay. As the elders record the final tape loops, the lingering chorus rises from the dust: "The rails have ended, so we blow the valves open."
